cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Plant virus host-range: data, analysis code and twelve-family phylogenies"
message: >-
  If you use this software or data, please cite both this repository and the
  associated manuscript.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Mi"
    given-names: "Xinrui"
abstract: >-
  Released analysis-ready datasets, final manuscript analysis code, derived analysis data, the twelve
  family phylogenies and supplementary tables (Data S1, Tables S1-S5) for an analysis of the global
  structure of plant virus host ranges. The resource covers 80,028 virus sequences and 83,034 curated
  virus-host associations spanning 76 virus families, 296 host families and 184 countries. Analyses
  cover host phylogenetic constraint across twelve virus families (6,010 tree tips, 999 permutations
  per family), arthropod-associated sequence evidence and documented vector transmission ecology,
  genus-host network structure, twelve prioritised genera, and a tomato spotted wilt virus (TSWV)
  case study. Plotting code for Figures 1-5 and Supplementary Figures S1-S5 is included.
keywords:
  - plant virus
  - host range
  - virus-host association
  - host relatedness
  - phylogenetic constraint
  - arthropod transmission
  - network analysis
  - Orthotospovirus
